doc:sch-1-sec-195af-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "195AF(2) Acts of false attribution of authorship of cinematograph film" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) It is an act of false attribution in relation to the director, producer or screenwriter of the film:  (a) to insert or affix, or to authorise the inserting or affixing of, a person’s name on the film or on a copy of the film in such a way as to imply falsely that the person is the director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of the film; or  (b) to deal with the film or a copy of the film if a person’s name has been so inserted or affixed on the film or a copy, as the case may be, and the attributor knows that the person is not the director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of the film; or  (c) to transmit the film as being a film of which a person is the director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, if the attributor knows that the person is not the director, producer or screenwriter of the film.  Schedule 1  Moral rights of authors" ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer .

concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ag a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "195AG Acts of false attribution of authorship of altered literary,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-195ag ;
    values:originalText "dramatic, musical or artistic work  (1) If the work is a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work that has been altered by a person other than the author of the work, it is an act of false attribution in relation to the author of the work:  (a) to deal with the work as so altered, as being the unaltered work of the author; or  (b) to deal with a reproduction of the work as so altered, as being a reproduction of the unaltered work of the author; if, to the knowledge of the attributor, it is not the unaltered work or a reproduction of the unaltered work, as the case may be, of the author.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the effect of the alteration is insubstantial; or  (b) the alteration was required by law to be made, or was otherwise necessary to avoid a breach of any law." ;
    skos:definition "dramatic, musical or artistic work  (1) If the work is a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work that has been altered by a person other than the author of the work, it is an act of false attribution in relation to the author of the work:  (a) to deal with the work as so altered, as being the unaltered work of the author; or  (b) to deal with a reproduction of the work as so altered, as being a reproduction of the unaltered work of the author; if, to the knowledge of the attributor, it is not the unaltered work or a reproduction of the unaltered work, as the case may be, of the author.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the effect of the alteration is insubstantial; or  (b) the alteration was required by law to be made, or was otherwise necessary to avoid a breach of any law."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "055bab7702b44d6f9fe72470a2f5245772a2baf4e582b6a44ca7265c29aa2b19" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ag-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ag-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf> ;
    dc:source "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.14" .
doc:sch-1-sec-195ag a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "195AG Acts of false attribution of authorship of altered literary," ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "dramatic, musical or artistic work  (1) If the work is a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work that has been altered by a person other than the author of the work, it is an act of false attribution in relation to the author of the work:  (a) to deal with the work as so altered, as being the unaltered work of the author; or  (b) to deal with a reproduction of the work as so altered, as being a reproduction of the unaltered work of the author; if, to the knowledge of the attributor, it is not the unaltered work or a reproduction of the unaltered work, as the case may be, of the author.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) the effect of the alteration is insubstantial; or  (b) the alteration was required by law to be made, or was otherwise necessary to avoid a breach of any law." ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer .

