    skos:definition "(1) If the work is a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work that has been altered by a person other than the author of the work, it is an act of false attribution in relation to the author of the work:  (a) to deal with the work as so altered, as being the unaltered work of the author; or  (b) to deal with a reproduction of the work as so altered, as being a reproduction of the unaltered work of the author; if, to the knowledge of the attributor, it is not the unaltered work or a reproduction of the unaltered work, as the case may be, of the author."@en ;
