concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ak a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "195AK Derogatory treatment of artistic work"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-195ak ;
    values:originalText "In this Part: derogatory treatment, in relation to an artistic work, means:  (a) the doing, in relation to the work, of anything that results in a material distortion of, the destruction or mutilation of, or a material alteration to, the work that is prejudicial to the author’s honour or reputation; or  (b) an exhibition in public of the work that is prejudicial to the author’s honour or reputation because of the manner or place in which the exhibition occurs; or  (c) the doing of anything else in relation to the work that is prejudicial to the author’s honour or reputation.  Schedule 1  Moral rights of authors" ;
    skos:definition "In this Part: derogatory treatment, in relation to an artistic work, means:  (a) the doing, in relation to the work, of anything that results in a material distortion of, the destruction or mutilation of, or a material alteration to, the work that is prejudicial to the author’s honour or reputation; or  (b) an exhibition in public of the work that is prejudicial to the author’s honour or reputation because of the manner or place in which the exhibition occurs; or  (c) the doing of anything else in relation to the work that is prejudicial to the author’s honour or reputation.  Schedule 1  Moral rights of authors"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3287c352640c2f607f1aee8b3259016d5ae0f0be734014229d8d2fbb11a795f8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Derogatory treatment of artistic work is prohibited." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
