;  (f) any practice, in the industry in which the film is used, that is relevant to the film or the use of the film;  (g) any practice contained in a voluntary code of practice, in the industry in which the film is used, that is relevant to the film or the use of the film;  (h) any difficulty or expense that would have been incurred as a result of identifying the maker;  (i) whether the film was made in the course of the employment of the director, producer or screenwriter." ;
