doc:sch-1-sec-195az-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "195AZ(1) Actions for infringement of moral rights" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to section 203, the relief that a court may grant in an action for an infringement of any of an author’s moral rights in respect of a work includes any one or more of the following:  (a) an injunction (subject to any terms that the court thinks fit);  Moral rights of authors  Schedule 1  (b) damages for loss resulting from the infringement;  (c) a declaration that a moral right of the author has been infringed;  (d) an order that the defendant make a public apology for the infringement;  (e) an order that any false attribution of authorship, or derogatory treatment, of the work be removed or reversed." ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer .

concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "195AZ(2) Actions for infringement of moral rights"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) In exercising its discretion as to the appropriate relief to be granted, the court may take into account any of the following:  (a) whether the defendant was aware, or ought reasonably to have been aware, of the author’s moral rights;  (b) the effect on the author’s honour or reputation resulting from any damage to the work;  (c) the number, and categories, of people who have seen or heard the work;  (d) anything done by the defendant to mitigate the effects of the infringement;  (e) if the moral right that was infringed was a right of attribution of authorship—any cost or difficulty that would have been associated with identifying the author;  (f) any cost or difficulty in removing or reversing any false attribution of authorship, or derogatory treatment, of the work." ;
    skos:definition "(2) In exercising its discretion as to the appropriate relief to be granted, the court may take into account any of the following:  (a) whether the defendant was aware, or ought reasonably to have been aware, of the author’s moral rights;  (b) the effect on the author’s honour or reputation resulting from any damage to the work;  (c) the number, and categories, of people who have seen or heard the work;  (d) anything done by the defendant to mitigate the effects of the infringement;  (e) if the moral right that was infringed was a right of attribution of authorship—any cost or difficulty that would have been associated with identifying the author;  (f) any cost or difficulty in removing or reversing any false attribution of authorship, or derogatory treatment, of the work."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3cc59b91ceef452fb2acd4b2c987b141e0f7e281c2c63b22c79418d4ad00e059" ;
    values:partOf concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may consider factors when granting relief for moral rights infringement. Damages recovered in one proceeding are taken into account in assessing damages in another proceeding arising out of the same operation or transaction. Decision of a court is final. Presumption of authorship for film director, producer or screenwriter" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf> ;
    dc:source "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.28" ;
    cml:asserts concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-norm .
