concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "195AZ(3) Actions for infringement of moral rights"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-195az-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) In deciding whether or not to grant an injunction under subsection (1), the court must consider whether the parties have made any attempt to negotiate a settlement of the action and whether it should adjourn the hearing or further hearing of the action for the purpose of giving the parties an appropriate opportunity to negotiate a settlement, whether through a process of mediation or otherwise." ;
    skos:definition "(3) In deciding whether or not to grant an injunction under subsection (1), the court must consider whether the parties have made any attempt to negotiate a settlement of the action and whether it should adjourn the hearing or further hearing of the action for the purpose of giving the parties an appropriate opportunity to negotiate a settlement, whether through a process of mediation or otherwise."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "135acb82df5ca8b5945c80418ac5a9894e6e9bf159d9b3545c1b7c88c07a0dec" ;
    values:partOf concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Appeal from a decision of a court under this Part Damages recovered in other proceedings are to be taken into account. Court must consider negotiating a settlement before granting an injunction." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf> ;
