concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "195AZ(4) Actions for infringement of moral rights"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The Federal Court of Australia has jurisdiction with respect to matters arising under this Part. 195AZD  Presumption as to subsistence of copyright  In an action brought under this Part for an infringement of a moral right in respect of a work, copyright is presumed to subsist in the work if the defendant does not put in issue the question whether copyright subsists in the work. 195AZE  Presumption as to subsistence of moral rights  In an action brought under this Part for an infringement of a moral right in respect of a work, if copyright is presumed or proved to have subsisted in the work when the infringement is alleged to have occurred, the moral right is presumed to have subsisted in the work at that time. 195AZF  Presumptions in relation to authorship of work" ;
    skos:definition "(4) The Federal Court of Australia has jurisdiction with respect to matters arising under this Part. 195AZD  Presumption as to subsistence of copyright  In an action brought under this Part for an infringement of a moral right in respect of a work, copyright is presumed to subsist in the work if the defendant does not put in issue the question whether copyright subsists in the work. 195AZE  Presumption as to subsistence of moral rights  In an action brought under this Part for an infringement of a moral right in respect of a work, if copyright is presumed or proved to have subsisted in the work when the infringement is alleged to have occurred, the moral right is presumed to have subsisted in the work at that time. 195AZF  Presumptions in relation to authorship of work"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5707faa27a02291be78c349d44318c7f653c79cbc93648155543dfda0d5ff71c" ;
    values:partOf concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Federal Court of Australia has jurisdiction over matters arising under this Part. Reduction of damages for screenwriters in moral rights infringement actions" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf> ;
    dc:source "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.28" ;
    cml:asserts concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-norm .
